  "label": "The Holocaust",
  "description": "A genocide during World War II in which Nazi Germany and its collaborators systematically murdered approximately six million Jews, along with millions of others including Roma, disabled individuals, Poles, Soviet prisoners of war, and others. The crematoriums depicted in the image were part of the Nazi death camps (e.g., Auschwitz-Birkenau) where bodies were incinerated to hide evidence of mass murder. Understanding this historical event is essential to interpret the text overlay's reference to 'the horrors of the Holocaust'.",
